# Production deploy = four-droplet only

When deploying FixitLab to production (`FixitLab Production` workflow):

- **ALWAYS** set `topology=four-droplet` (never leave the default / never use `single`)
- Prefer `action=deploy`, `wire_existing=true`, `cloud_provider=digitalocean`, `hosting_target=droplets`, `create_server=false`
- Do **not** trigger a bare `gh workflow run "FixitLab Production"` without `-f topology=four-droplet` — that historically ran the single-droplet path and skipped all `[4D]` jobs

Example:

```bash
gh workflow run "FixitLab Production" --ref main \
  -f action=deploy \
  -f topology=four-droplet \
  -f wire_existing=true \
  -f cloud_provider=digitalocean \
  -f hosting_target=droplets \
  -f create_server=false
```
